                        What is Euler's totient ϕ(N)?
                    </p>
                    <p class=" coming-soon-regular" style="background-color: rgba(151, 240, 42, 0.13);;">
                        <br>
                        🔑d≡e<sup>-1</sup>mod &phi;(N)
                        <br>
                        <br>
                        <strong>Euler's Totient Function</strong><br>
                        &phi;(N) = (p − 1) × (q − 1)*<br>
                        <br>Caz general:
                        <br>N = p₁<sup>k₁</sup> × p₂<sup>k₂</sup> × ... × pₙ<sup>kₙ</sup><br>
                        &phi;(N) = N &times; &prod;(1 &minus; 1/p)<br>
                        <br>

                        <br>Explictie formula:<br>
                        N = p * q<br>
&phi;(N) = N × (1 - 1/p) × (1 - 1/q)<br>
&ensp;= p × q × (1 - 1/p) × (1 - 1/q)<br>
&ensp;= p × q × ((p - 1)/p) × ((q - 1)/q)<br>
&ensp;= (p - 1)(q - 1)
                        <br>
                        <br>
                    </p>
                    <p class=" coming-soon-regular">
                        &phi;(N) = N × (1 - 1/N)= N - 1<br>
                        => 🔑d≡e<sup>-1</sup>mod N-1
                    </p>
